From: khegazy <address removed>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:41:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Calibrate the forced 2D turbulence case on 1024^2 pilots:
 Re 40000, drag 5e-5, variance 2.55e-11

The design values (Re 2700, drag 2.26e-4, variance 1.5e-10) gave no cascade: viscosity
removed 77% of the injection at the forcing scale and the spectrum peaked at the forcing
shell. At Re 40000 the run is stable and 74% of the injection reaches the drag. Weakening
the drag moved the arrest of the inverse cascade from shell 12 (2.26e-4) to shells 4 to 6
(5e-5), where the compensated spectrum is flat from shell 6 to 30 and the lowest shells do
not grow over 150000 steps. The variance scales with the drag to hold the rms speed near
Ma c_s. The case is renamed for its Reynolds number; its header records the pilots.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <address removed>
---
 ...aml => Re-40k_Ma-1en1_forced_drag_2d.yaml} | 26 +++++++++++++------
 .../initialize.py                             |  2 +-
 tests/simulations/test_case_smokes.py         |  2 +-
 3 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)
 rename simulations/homogeneous_isotropic_turbulence/{Re-2700_Ma-1en1_forced_drag_2d.yaml => Re-40k_Ma-1en1_forced_drag_2d.yaml} (58%)

diff --git a/simulations/homogeneous_isotropic_turbulence/Re-2700_Ma-1en1_forced_drag_2d.yaml b/simulations/homogeneous_isotropic_turbulence/Re-40k_Ma-1en1_forced_drag_2d.yaml
similarity index 58%
rename from simulations/homogeneous_isotropic_turbulence/Re-2700_Ma-1en1_forced_drag_2d.yaml
rename to simulations/homogeneous_isotropic_turbulence/Re-40k_Ma-1en1_forced_drag_2d.yaml
index 8cf132f54..4498f7069 100644
--- a/simulations/homogeneous_isotropic_turbulence/Re-2700_Ma-1en1_forced_drag_2d.yaml
+++ b/simulations/homogeneous_isotropic_turbulence/Re-40k_Ma-1en1_forced_drag_2d.yaml
@@ -1,21 +1,31 @@
 # Statistically stationary forced 2D turbulence with a large-scale drag (double cascade).
 #
-# Random-mode forcing confined to the shell 31 <= |n| <= 33 (forcing scale 32 cells on
+# Random-mode forcing confined to the shell 31 <= |n| <= 33 (forcing wavelength 32 cells on
 # 1024^2) and a linear drag (a negative constant rate of the linear law) that removes the
 # energy the inverse cascade carries to large scales, so energy and enstrophy become
 # statistically steady (Boffetta and Ecke, Annu. Rev. Fluid Mech. 44, 427 (2012); Boffetta
 # and Musacchio, Phys. Rev. E 82, 016307 (2010), Eq. 1). Plain BGK with the polynomial
 # equilibrium, as the shipped forced cases: entropic BGK with a body force is much slower
-# and its stabilizer measures the force. The drag rate and the forcing variance were
-# calibrated on a pilot run for a stationary rms speed near Ma c_s and an arrest scale
-# u'/alpha well inside the box.
+# and its stabilizer measures the force.
+#
+# Calibrated on 1024^2 pilots (2026-11-27), from the design Re 2700, drag 2.26e-4,
+# variance 1.5e-10:
+#   - Re 2700 removed 77% of the injection by viscosity at the forcing scale; the spectrum
+#     peaked at the forcing shell, so there was neither an inverse nor a direct range.
+#     Re 40000 (tau - 1/2 = 4.4e-3) ran stably and passes 74% of the injection to the drag.
+#   - The drag sets the arrest wavenumber: 2.26e-4, 1e-4, 7e-5 and 5e-5 arrested the inverse
+#     cascade near shells 12, 9, 9 and 4 to 6. At 5e-5 the compensated spectrum is flat from
+#     shell 6 to 30 and the lowest shells do not grow over 150000 steps (no condensate).
+#   - The variance scales with the drag to hold the rms speed near Ma c_s: 2.55e-11 gives
+#     u' = 0.055 (rms Mach 0.096 on c_s).
+# Energy relaxes on 1/(2 alpha) = 10000 steps; the pilot settled within 30000 to 50000.
 defaults:
   - /physics: weakly_compressible_isothermal_fluids
   - /collision: bgk
   - /lattice: d2q9
   - /equilibrium_closure/numeric@simulate_equilibrium_closure.F: polynomial
   - /forecast: very_long
-id: Re-2700_Ma-1en1_forced_drag_2d
+id: Re-40k_Ma-1en1_forced_drag_2d
 group: homogeneous_isotropic_turbulence
 features: [turbulence]
 units: lattice
@@ -32,7 +42,7 @@ discretization:
 physics:
   parameters:
     mach: 0.1
-    reynolds: 2700
+    reynolds: 40000
     reference:
       density: 1.0
   output_variables:
@@ -43,11 +53,11 @@ physics:
       - type: random_modes
         seed: 1729
         correlation_time: 10.0
-        variance: 1.5e-10
+        variance: 2.55e-11
         minimum_mode: 31.0
         maximum_mode: 33.0
       - type: linear
-        rate: -2.26e-4
+        rate: -5.0e-5
         rate_policy: constant
 initial_conditions:
   density: 1.0
